stant","model":"Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B-Instruct","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good, I've confirmed the baseline score of 0.44514. Now I'll implement a feature engineering strategy that leverages the relationships between the categorical variables. Based on the problem description, approval depends on how often a (role, resource) pair occurs and on the manager's number of requests.\n\nLet me implement a pipeline with engineered features:\n\n"}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0}}},{"type":"assistant","uuid":"3af69210-f42a-4921-ade3-9602cb7e73e2","session_id":"28043fdc-8196-4988-806f-e08dd6d0b2ef","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"3af69210-f42a-4921-ade3-9602cb7e73e2","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B-Instruct","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_c75c31af328e4e4994a8c2ee","name":"edit","input":{"file_path":"/home/yarin.b/projects/excel_magic/artifacts/runs/20261002T174414Z_J6_qwen-code_synth_entities/workspace/pipeline.py","old_string":"\"\"\"Candidate data pipeline around a FROZEN tabular foundation model.\n\nThe harness calls, in order:\n  1. preprocess(X_train, y_train, X_test)        -> X_train, y_train, X_test   (cleaning, target transform)\n  2. engineer(X_train, y_train, X_test)          -> X_train, X_test            (feature engineering, <= 500 cols)\n  3. sample(X_train, y_train, X_test, max_rows)  -> list of index arrays       (context views; each view is fit separately\n                                                                                 and predictions are averaged)\n  4. frozen model fit/predict per view (never edit this part; MODEL_KWARGS tunes the constructor)\n  5. postprocess(pred, y_train_orig, X_test)     -> pred                       (invert target transforms, calibrate)\n\n`pred` is a pandas DataFrame of class probabilities (columns = class labels) for classification, or a\npandas Series for regression. `y_train_orig` is the untransformed training target. All inputs are pandas\nobjects; X_train / X_test share columns. Do not read any file other than the ones in this directory.\n\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nMODEL_KWARGS = {}  # constructor settings for the frozen model; {} keeps the defaults\n\n\ndef preprocess(X_train, y_train, X_test):\n    return X_train, y_train, X_test\n\n\ndef engineer(X_train, y_train, X_test):\n    return X_train, X_test\n\n\ndef sample(X_train, y_train, X_test, max_rows):\n    return [np.arange(len(X_train))]  # one context view with all training rows\n\n\ndef postprocess(pred, y_train_orig, X_test):\n    return pred","new_string":"\"\"\"Candidate data pipeline around a FROZEN tabular foundation model.\n\nThe harness calls, in order:\n  1. preprocess(X_train, y_train, X_test)        -> X_train, y_train, X_test   (cleaning, target transform)\n  2. engineer(X_train, y_train, X_test)          -> X_train, X_test            (feature engineering, <= 500 cols)\n  3. sample(X_train, y_train, X_test, max_rows)  -> list of index arrays       (context views; each view is fit separately\n                                                                                 and predictions are averaged)\n  4. frozen model fit/predict per view (never edit this part; MODEL_KWARGS tunes the constructor)\n  5. postprocess(pred, y_train_orig, X_test)     -> pred                       (invert target transforms, calibrate)\n\n`pred` is a pandas DataFrame of class probabilities (columns = class labels) for classification, or a\npandas Series for regression. `y_train_orig` is the untransformed training target. All inputs are pandas\nobjects; X_train / X_test share columns. Do not read any file other than the ones in this directory.\n\"\"\"\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nMODEL_KWARGS = {}  # constructor settings for the frozen model; {} keeps the defaults\n\n\ndef preprocess(X_train, y_train, X_test):\n    return X_train, y_train, X_test\n\n\ndef engineer(X_train, y_train, X_test):\n    # Create a combined dataframe for easier manipulation\n    X_train_combined = X_train.copy()\n    X_test_combined = X_test.copy()\n    \n    # Add the target variable to the training set for groupby operations\n    X_train_combined['approved'] = y_train\n    \n    # 1. Frequency of (role, resource) pairs\n    role_resource_counts = X_train_combined.groupby(['role_id', 'resource_id']).size().reset_index(name='role_resource_count')\n    X_train_combined = X_train_combined.merge(role_resource_counts, on=['role_id', 'resource_id'], how='left')\n    X_test_combined = X_test_combined.merge(role_resource_counts, on=['role_id', 'resource_id'], how='left')\n    \n    # 2. Frequency of managers\n    manager_counts = X_train_combined.groupby('manager_id').size().reset_index(name='manager_request_count')\n    X_train_combined = X_train_combined.merge(manager_counts, on='manager_id', how='left')\n    X_test_combined = X_test_combined.merge(manager_counts, on='manager_id', how='left')\n    \n    # 3. Role-frequency interaction\n    role_counts = X_train_combined.groupby('role_id').size().reset_index(name='role_count')\n    X_train_combined = X_train_combined.merge(role_counts, on='role_id', how='left')\n    X_test_combined = X_test_combined.merge(role_counts, on='role_id', how='left')\n    \n    # 4. Resource-frequency interaction  \n    resource_counts = X_train_combined.groupby('resource_id').size().reset_index(name='resource_count')\n    X_train_combined = X_train_combined.merge(resource_counts, on='resource_id', how='left')\n    X_test_combined = X_test_combined.merge(resource_counts, on='resource_id', how='left')\n    \n    # 5. Normalize frequencies to prevent extreme values\n    X_train_combined['role_resource_freq'] = X_train_combined['role_resource_count'] / len(X_train_combined)\n    X_test_combined['role_resource_freq'] = X_test_combined['role_resource_count'] / len(X_train_combined)\n    \n    # 6. Manager request count ratio (normalized)\n    X_train_combined['manager_request_ratio'] = X_train_combined['manager_request_count'] / len(X_train_combined)\n    X_test_combined['manager_request_ratio'] = X_test_combined['manager_request_count'] / len(X_train_combined)\n    \n    # 7. Role count ratio (normalized)\n    X_train_combined['role_ratio'] = X_train_combined['role_count'] / len(X_train_combined)\n    X_test_combined['role_ratio'] = X_test_combined['role_count'] / len(X_train_combined)\n    \n    # 8. Resource count ratio (normalized)\n    X_train_combined['resource_ratio'] = X_train_combined['resource_count'] / len(X_train_combined)\n    X_test_combined['resource_ratio'] = X_test_combined['resource_count'] / len(X_train_combined)\n    \n    # Remove the target variable from the training set\n    y_train_new = X_train_combined.pop('approved')\n    \n    # Return updated dataframes\n    return X_train_combined, X_test_combined\n\n\ndef sample(X_train, y_train, X_test, max_rows):\n    return [np.arange(len(X_train))]  # one context view with all training rows\n\n\ndef postprocess(pred, y_train_orig, X_test):\n    return pred"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","usage":{"input_tokens":21279,"output_tokens":1526,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"total_tokens":22805}}},{"type":"user","uuid":"6602e1e0-68be-47bf-9b59-33e82978e2cd","session_id":"28043fdc-8196-4988-806f-e08dd6d0b2ef","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_c75c31af328e4e4994a8c2ee","is_error":false,"content":"The file: /home/yarin.b/projects/excel_magic/artifacts/runs/20261002T174414Z_J6_qwen-code_synth_entities/workspace/pipeline.py has been updated. Showing lines 22-77 of 82 from the edited file:\n\n---\n\n    return X_train, y_train, X_test\n\n\ndef engineer(X_train, y_train, X_test):\n    # Create a combined dataframe for easier manipulation\n    X_train_combined = X_train.copy()\n    X_test_combined = X_test.copy()\n    \n    # Add the target variable to the training set for groupby operations\n    X_train_